[2026-09-21 14:31:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 016] STEP PURPOSE
[2026-09-21 14:31:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 016] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-21 14:31:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 016]   TEP / Planet-9 -- step b8: distance-aware footprint null
[2026-09-21 14:31:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 016]   Step b5 reconstructed the detached sample's own discovery
[2026-09-21 14:31:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 016]   footprint.  Step b7 flagged the remaining caveat: the empirical
[2026-09-21 14:31:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 016]   null assumed a radius-independent footprint, while distant
[2026-09-21 14:31:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 016]   objects are found by fewer, deeper surveys -- the footprint may
[2026-09-21 14:31:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 016]   NARROW with a.  This step measures that directly and rebuilds
[2026-09-21 14:31:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 016]   the nulls conditioned on each object's own discovery geometry.
[2026-09-21 14:31:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 016]   Every provisional designation gives the discovery half-month ->
[2026-09-21 14:31:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 016]   opposition longitude lam_opp.  The footprint-versus-distance
[2026-09-21 14:31:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 016]   profile, the convolution decomposition varpi = lam_opp + Delta,
[2026-09-21 14:31:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 016]   and the pairing test are all computed from real metadata.
[2026-09-21 14:31:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 016]   D1  Footprint vs a: R(lam_opp) and mean direction per a-bin.
[2026-09-21 14:31:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 016]   The profile shows whether distant discoveries really come
[2026-09-21 14:31:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 016]   from a narrower sky.
[2026-09-21 14:31:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 016]   D2  The convolution test: varpi_i = lam_opp_i + Delta_i.
[2026-09-21 14:31:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 016]   Under pure footprint manufacture Delta is a pointing smear
[2026-09-21 14:31:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 016]   independent of lam_opp; the observed pairing is then a
[2026-09-21 14:31:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 016]   typical shuffle and R(varpi) sits inside the shuffle
[2026-09-21 14:31:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 016]   distribution.  Under intrinsic clustering the pairing must
[2026-09-21 14:31:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 016]   compensate (objects found off-axis need larger Delta to land
[2026-09-21 14:31:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 016]   on the axis), pushing observed R(varpi) to the edge of the
[2026-09-21 14:31:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 016]   shuffle null.  Both marginals come from the detached sample
[2026-09-21 14:31:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 016]   itself -- no transfer assumption.
[2026-09-21 14:31:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 016]   D3  Footprint-conditional (Om,w) null: for each detached object
[2026-09-21 14:31:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 016]   draw a control object's (Om,w) pair from controls whose
[2026-09-21 14:31:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 016]   lam_opp lies within +-30 deg of that object's own.  This
[2026-09-21 14:31:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 016]   reproduces the MEASURED detached footprint and the empirical
[2026-09-21 14:31:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 016]   elements<->footprint map simultaneously -- the tightest
[2026-09-21 14:31:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 016]   achievable catalog null for R(varpi).
[2026-09-21 14:31:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 016]   D4  Same conditional null for the pole tilt (resolves the b7
[2026-09-21 14:31:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 016]   caveat): draw (Om,i) per object from lam_opp-matched
[2026-09-21 14:31:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 016]   controls, compute the coherent mean-pole tilt.  Does the
[2026-09-21 14:31:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 016]   detached sample's narrow footprint alone generate its 6.4 deg
[2026-09-21 14:31:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 016]   coherent tilt toward az ~ 50 deg?
[2026-09-21 14:31:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 016]   Caveats: lam_opp remains an opposition proxy for true discovery
[2026-09-21 14:31:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 016]   longitude; the D3/D4 conditional map is estimated on control
[2026-09-21 14:31:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 016]   objects at a < 150 AU whose discovery geometry (all orbital
[2026-09-21 14:31:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 016]   phases) differs from near-perihelion-dominated distant
[2026-09-21 14:31:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 016]   discoveries -- the D2 pairing test uses only the detached
[2026-09-21 14:31:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 016]   sample's own marginals and carries no such assumption.
